# Bagisto Performance

Reference: `docs/performance-analysis.md`

## Database

- Add indexes for columns used in `WHERE`, `JOIN`, `ORDER BY` — use `Schema::hasIndex()` guards in migrations.
- Avoid `LIKE '%term%'` on large tables; prefer FULLTEXT (`MATCH...AGAINST`) for latin search, exact match for slugs (`url_key`).
- EAV (`product_attribute_values`): minimize self-joins; prefer `product_flat` / index tables for read paths.
- New migrations go in `database/migrations/` with reversible `down()`.

## Queries & Code

- No N+1: eager-load in DataGrids (`formatRecords` batch preload), listings (`with([...])`), admin loops.
- DataGrid column closures must not call `Repository->find()` per row.
- Use repositories; select only needed columns in heavy reports.
- Dispatch heavy work (`ShouldQueue` jobs: price/inventory/ES index) — never block HTTP with `sync` in production.

## Production Config (when deploying)

- `QUEUE_CONNECTION=redis`, `CACHE_STORE=redis`, `SESSION_DRIVER=redis`
- `APP_DEBUG=false`, run `php artisan optimize`
- Enable Elasticsearch when catalog > ~1,000 SKUs

## After Changes

- Run `vendor/bin/pint --dirty` on PHP changes.
- Clear caches if config/routes change: `php artisan optimize:clear`
